# OSE-1030 — @ocr/flags via GitHub Packages (registry), replacing the file: clone-dance.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# WHY: the old `file:../packages/flags` link required cloning the hub repo into a
# self-hosted-PERSISTENT cache (scripts/ci-stage-ocr-workspace.sh). On ephemeral
# managed (ubuntu) runners that link is "invalid" to `npm ls --all`, breaking the
# S0 SBOM (CycloneDX) with ELSPROBLEMS. Publishing @ocr/flags to a registry removes
# the file: link and is supply-chain-safer (a pinned version, not clone-at-build).
#
# NAMING: GitHub Packages routes by npm scope == owning org login, so the package
# publishes as @ourcommunityrituals/flags. package.json consumes it under the
# ORIGINAL import name via an npm alias:
#     "@ocr/flags": "npm:@ourcommunityrituals/flags@0.1.0"
# Source keeps importing @ocr/flags (Invariant #22 intact) and the bytes are
# byte-identical (published from the same packages/flags tree; parity verified).
#
# SCOPE: ONLY @ocr/flags is migrated — it is the SOLE SBOM `npm ls` breaker.
# @ocr/ui and @ocr/data-provider INTENTIONALLY remain file: (react/ui is not the
# breaker; migrating them + retiring ci-stage-ocr-workspace.sh is a follow-up).
# Do not re-litigate this scope.
#
# AUTH:
#   - CI: NODE_AUTH_TOKEN = GITHUB_TOKEN with `permissions: packages: read`.
#   - Local dev: add to your ~/.npmrc a line
#       //npm.pkg.github.com/:_authToken=<a PAT with read:packages>
#     (file: "just worked" offline; the registry needs a read token — one-time.)
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
@ourcommunityrituals:registry=https://npm.pkg.github.com
//npm.pkg.github.com/:_authToken=${NODE_AUTH_TOKEN}
